    "turn_text": "Yeah, yeah, I love her. You know, thank you for giving that level set. And I'm just going to say this real quick before I answer your question. Please. I think as black people in general, we have always been the ones that have never shot away from hard work. We aren't given positions on boards. We're not given positions in government. We're not given positions in schools like we're not the legacies. They get admitted to these institutions. We've had to work and earn every single thing that we've ever gotten. And the fact that the vice president is absolutely committed to going out and earning the votes, taking her fight straight to the people. I mean, you know, I think I don't sleep and then I think about her schedule and then I'm like, I'm like, but she got a pj. So",
